# Global gitignore. Git reads this path by default — no core.excludesFile needed,
# it is the XDG fallback ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore). Rules here apply to EVERY
# repo on the machine, so keep them to things that are never anyone's source.

# Backlog.md's task folder, when you keep the board out of the project's history.
# The DOT-prefixed spelling on purpose: Backlog.md also supports a plain `backlog/`,
# but globally ignoring that would hide legitimately-named directories in unrelated
# repos — Backlog.md's own repo keeps its tasks in `backlog/`. If you use the default
# name, put it in that project's own .gitignore instead of here.
.backlog/
